by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-14T07:46:43Z

Rebased on 8.2 and squashed the three commits; no code changes were needed.

@Spomky, @derrabus: the BC concern is addressed. The automatic violation is gated on `message`, which is a new option defaulting to `null`, so no existing constraint can reach it. Checked against the shapes you were worried about:

```
returns false, no message                  => 0 violations
adds violation via $context + returns false => 1 violation  (own)
adds violation via $context, returns nothing => 1 violation  (own)
returns false WITH message                 => 1 violation  (auto)
returns true WITH message                  => 0 violations
adds violation + returns false WITH message => 2 violations (own, auto)
```

The last line is the only way to get two, and it takes opting into `message` and also building your own, which is a deliberate combination rather than something existing code falls into. The reverted test fixtures @derrabus pointed at as the tell are indeed all back to their original state.

The PHP 8.5 fixture is already handled too: `testClosureInAttribute` carries `#[RequiresPhp('>=8.5.0')]`, so `CallbackTestWithClosure` is never autoloaded on older runtimes and never parsed. Verified by running the suite on both: 5280 tests green on 8.4 and on 8.5.

Only thing left is the docs PR, since `message` is new public API on a widely used constraint.

