by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-14T08:01:14Z

The exception now names the target, like the other Callback ones do:

```
The callback targeted by the Callback constraint on "App\Entity\Order::$deliveryDate" must return a boolean when the "message" option is set, "int" returned.
```

It uses the class and property from the execution context when there is one, falls back to the property path otherwise, and drops the fragment entirely when validating a bare value with no context, so the message never reads `on ""`. Two tests cover the class::$property and property-path forms. Validator is green at 5283 tests on 8.4 and 8.5.
